title: Put fields before the body and drop desc:
effort: M
area: format
created: 2026-09-17T04:39:14Z
updated: 2026-09-17T04:39:14Z
handoff:

desc: was derived data a hand-edit could falsify, and only check would ever
notice. It turned out not to be a necessary cost: it existed to serve one
layout choice — fields after the body — and that choice was what created the
derived data.

The layout is now three header lines, the project's fields, a blank line,
then the body to the end of the file. The body ends at EOF, which nothing
can spoof. The fields end at the first blank after line 3, a boundary that
sits ahead of the body, so the delimiter-spoofing objection that justified
desc: does not apply once the delimiter moves in front.

Every bounded read survived and reading fields got cheaper — a scan from the
top rather than a seek past the body. What was given up is a fixed line
number for the start of the body, which now depends on how many fields a
ticket has; nothing stores it, so nothing can disagree with it.

Appending to a body now needs no bookkeeping at all, which is what 19's
retraction made the central operation, and principle 5 lost its only
exception. pidly edit in 10 is now a convenience rather than a correctness
requirement.

Migrated all 20 tickets, both generated documents, this repo's schema and
every suite. Tests cover a body containing blank lines, a body line that
reads as a field, an empty body, and appending by hand.
